Loom: let register allocation see instruction operand preferences (matrix operand banks), not only final numbering.
On gfx1151 an iu4 WMMA costs 16, 17 or 18 cycles by its A/B/C start banks (16 iff {A, B} = {C+2, C+3} mod 4); the
numbering pass can only permute packed blocks without regressing any use and cannot reach that layout. Allocation now
also tries a first fit whose queries see instruction uses, grouped across whole-value copies, moves and edges (an
accumulator seeded by a copy then sees its WMMAs), and keeps it only without spills and without a lower residency
tier (attention wmma would lose a wave). Adds the gfx1151 iu4 WMMA qualification. Bit-identical results;
yah gu 17.47 -> 16.19 predicted cycles/WMMA, pp2048 GEMM cycles -3.9%.
